   "text": "This structure is a cyclosporin A\u2013dasatinib conjugate. I did not derive the stereochemistry from the wedges and hashes. I took the cyclosporin A stereocentres from its known SMILES, and I did not check each one against the drawing.\n\n**Macrocycle (cyclosporin A core).** The undecapeptide ring is cyclo[MeBmt-Abu-Sar-MeLeu-Val-MeLeu-Ala-D-Ala-MeLeu-MeLeu-MeVal], with the N-methylated residues drawn as in the image.\n\n**Modified MeBmt side chain.** The usual butenyl group is replaced. From the hydroxylated carbon the chain runs CH(CH3)\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O), and that carbonyl is an amide to a piperazine nitrogen.\n\n**Dasatinib-type part.**\n- The piperazine's other nitrogen is bonded to C6 of a 2-methylpyrimidine.\n- The pyrimidine C4 carries an NH that links to C2 of a thiazole.\n- The thiazole C5 carries a C(=O)NH group attached to a 2-chloro-6-methylphenyl ring. I ignored the stray dot at the right edge of the image.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@H]1C(=O)N(CC(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N1)[C@@H]([C@H](C)CCCC(=O)N1CCN(CC1)c1cc(Nc2ncc(s2)C(=O)Nc2c(C)cccc2Cl)nc(C)n1)O)C)C(C)C)C)CC(C)C)C)C)C)CC(C)C)C(C)C)CC(C)C)C"
